```ts
test("built dist lexicon HTML keeps the etymology handler when dist/ is present", () => {
    const distLexicon = resolve(process.cwd(), "dist/lexicon");
    if (!existsSync(distLexicon)) {
      expect(true).toBe(true);
      return;
    }
    ...
});
```

The task wants me to replace `if (!existsSync(distLexicon)) { expect(true).toBe(true); return }` with `it.skipIf(!existsSync(distLexicon))` or `describe.skipIf`. 

However, there's a subtlety: `existsSync` check is currently done inside the test body. With `it.skipIf`, the condition is evaluated at definition time (top-level), not inside the test. So I need to compute the dist existence before defining the test.

Let me check the vitest version and whether `it.skipIf` is supported. `test.skipIf` / `it.skipIf` is available in Vitest 0.23+. Let me check the site's package.json.

Also, `distLexicon` depends on `process.cwd()`. In the test, `process.cwd()` would be the site dir when running `cd site && npx vitest run`. But wait — `resolve(process.cwd(), "dist/lexicon")` — when running from site dir, this resolves to `site/dist/lexicon`. That's fine.

Let me check how `it.skipIf` works: `it.skipIf(condition)(name, fn)`. So the check must be evaluated at module definition time.

Let me check the vitest config and other test files to see if `skipIf` is already used in the codebase, to follow conventions.

